# ── build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.o
*.obj
*.exe
*.out
inop
build/
probe
probe.exe

# ── KEY MATERIAL — never commit these ───────────────────────────────────
# Wheel files and key sheets are the secret. Committing them to a public
# repo is the exact failure the whole design is meant to avoid: it hands an
# analyst the machine's wiring and the day's settings in one place.
#
# The data files became JSON in 2.3.0 and the plain-text names are still
# listed below them: a converted install has both on disk, and either one
# committed is the same permanent compromise. *.json is deliberately not
# blanket-ignored (CMakePresets.json and vcpkg.json are tracked), so every
# key-material JSON file has to be named here explicitly. Anything new
# that holds wiring, notches or a key belongs on this list the day it is
# invented.
inop_rotors.json
inop_reflectors.json
inop_keysheet.json
inop_settings.json
inop_wheels.txt
inop_keysheet.txt
inop.settings
*.settings
*.keysheet
setup/

# The GUI Save Setup panel writes master_key into JSON (to_json() in
# gui_config_store.cpp). Every one of those files lands in setup/, which
# the line above already covers whole — this states the rule that line
# only implies, so moving kDir cannot quietly start publishing key
# material. *.json is deliberately not blanket-ignored: CMakePresets.json
# and vcpkg.json are tracked and belong in the repo.
setup/*.json

# ── local application preferences ───────────────────────────────────────
# Written by the GUI settings screen: theme, colourblind mode, window mode
# and typeface. Not key material and not secret, but it describes one
# machine and one operator, so it has no business being in the repo. Note
# the *.json exception above still applies — this file is named
# explicitly, not covered by a wildcard.
inop.gui.json

# ── generated benchmark output ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Timing columns are machine/run-specific — committing them just churns the
# diff on every re-run for no benefit.
benchmark.csv

# ── editor / OS noise ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── local backup mirrors ────────────────────────────────────────────────
/WorldEngine-backup.git/

# ── untracked by intent, now by rule ────────────────────────────────────
# Both were untracked by convention only, which is not a rule. maria.txt
# is the roadmap. .claude/ holds local absolute paths and permission
# grants; it is currently caught by a machine-local global ignore file
# that does not travel with a clone, so the repo has to say it too.
maria.txt
.claude/

# ── working notes, not a published document ─────────────────────────────
# DESIGN.md is a scratchpad for reasoning in progress, not a deliverable.
# Untracked deliberately by the owner on this branch (it had been tracked
# since the project started). Nothing written here should cite it.
DESIGN.md

# ── screenshots a scripted run takes of itself ──────────────────────────
# `shot <name>` in a GUI script writes gui-shots/<name>.png next to
# wherever the binary was run from. They are evidence for one session, not
# something the repository should carry.
gui-shots/

*.md
!/README.md
!/audio/README.md
!/benchmark/corpus/SOURCES.md
/.agents/
/.codex/
/Jobs/
/measurements/
/screenshots/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
